Astigmatism is one of those monsters that started off weak, but gained buff after buff throughout the game's lifespan. Starting with 3/10 for 10G, its first buff was in '''Alpha 2.7''', where its cost dropped by 1G. '''Beta 4.2''' gave it +1 ATK and both '''Beta 4.8''' and '''Beta 5.3''' dropped its cost by 1G again. This left it at 4/10 for 7G.
[[File:Astigmatism (Beta 22.0).png|thumb|234x234px|Beta 22.0]]
During this time, it also had Disarmed, but '''Beta 7.1''' removed that at the cost of 1 ATK, dropping it back to 3. It also gained -2 HP with this, making this the first time its HP was changed. '''Beta 22.0''' buffed its effect again, as it will now add a [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Loox Loox] to your hand if there wasn't a monster in front of it. '''Beta 49.0''' gave it another -2 HP, but also reduced its cost by another 1G, leaving it at 3/6 for 6G. '''Beta 56.1''' revamped the card, giving it back its 7 cost and also +2 ATK, but trashing its turn start effect and replacing it with both an aura and a magic effect. Whenever it killed a monster, it added a [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Loox Loox] to your hand. Its Magic effect was akin to [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Vulkin Vulkin]'s, dealing 2 DMG. Its aura ability could trigger from its Magic ability, but also from attacking and killing or counterattacking a monster. 

